pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% Positive-direction companion of `incorrect/enumeration_soli_undercount`, and
% the scope line of that fix: `ENUMERATION_PARTIAL n` claims only that at least
% `n` projected solutions were witnessed. No rule ever adds models, so the `solx`
% below really did witness a distinct projected solution of the original problem
% and the claim survives the `soli`. Only the COMPLETE leg is guarded.
f 1;
solx x1 ~x2;
soli ~x1 x2;
pol 1 2 + 3 +;
output NONE;
conclusion ENUMERATION_PARTIAL 1;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
